        "id": 1047255
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-22T18:43:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This behavior feels like it belongs in the Zygote instead of a helper object.  Is there a reason that this logic is here instead?",
      "revId": "92ca13cba2f86c59f8ee9572bb367b2a80f2a2b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d4b32be4_bc17eded",
        "filename": "core/java/com/android/internal/os/ZygoteCommandBuffer.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 166,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042828
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-23T03:06:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At some level, I agree with you. It is a little weird that we draw the boundaries differently depending on how commands are executed. And I\u0027ve thought about doing as you suggest. But I think the alternative is likely to be worse, with wider interfaces. The ZygoteCommandBuffer data structure was really designed primarily to support this method. To separate this out, we\u0027d basically have to export the core NativeCommandBuffer data structure so that it\u0027s accessible from the Zygote native implementation. And even then, isSimpleForkCommand would seem out of place.\n\nAnd in a strong sense, it is really an operation on a ZygoteCommandBuffer.\n\nI changed the heading comment for the class to make this model a little clearer.",
      "parentUuid": "6e141526_b36daad2",
      "revId": "92ca13cba2f86c59f8ee9572bb367b2a80f2a2b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ef93b12d_9ada8b0b",
        "filename": "core/java/com/android/internal/os/ZygoteCommandBuffer.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 166,
      "author": {
        "id": 1047255
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-23T20:21:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would still strongly prefer this logic be in the Zygote class, but not enough to continue pressing the issue beyond this comment.  I think that keeping all of the logic related to forking new processes in the same place is important, even if it means turning the native ZygoteCommandBuffer object into a POD.\n\nWe\u0027re trading conceptual locality for encapsulation of a single object that is used by a single method/function.",
      "parentUuid": "d4b32be4_bc17eded",
      "revId": "92ca13cba2f86c59f8ee9572bb367b2a80f2a2b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
